    "comment": "Single source of truth for artwork shown in the gallery. Artwork is display only; there is no price, no wishlist and no purchase path. Add one object per work to the artworks array. Required: id, medium (must match a slug in gallery.json mediumPages), titleEn, titleZh, images. Optional: year (four-digit integer; omit it for an undated work and the card renders n.d.), sizeRange (small|medium|large|very-large), assigned from the longest side of the physical work and aligned to the standard stretched-canvas sizes an artist buys off the shelf, so every common size falls in exactly one band. Bands are continuous and bounded on the gaps between standard sizes; a size on a boundary belongs to the larger band. small is longest side under 16 in / 40 cm (e.g. 8x10, 9x12, 11x14, 12x12 in; 20x25, 25x30, 30x30 cm); medium is 16 to under 30 in / 40 to under 75 cm (e.g. 16x20, 18x24, 20x24, 24x24 in; 40x50, 50x60, 50x70 cm); large is 30 to under 48 in / 75 to under 120 cm (e.g. 24x30, 24x36, 30x40, 36x36 in; 60x80, 70x90, 80x100 cm); very-large is 48 in / 120 cm and up (e.g. 36x48, 40x60, 48x60 in; 90x120, 100x150 cm); colors (array), style (abstract|figurative|realist), dimensionsEn, dimensionsZh. Each entry in images needs src, width, height, view, altEn and altZh, plus source for provenance. view is front (the work photographed face on, cropped to its edges), in-situ (the work where it hangs, never cropped) or detail (one part of the work at close range, never cropped). The first image is the one the grid shows; when a front photograph exists it must come first, and a work with no front photograph leads with its in-situ shot followed by details. width and height are the real pixel dimensions of the file and are rendered as width/height attributes so the browser reserves layout space before the image loads. An in-situ photograph showing several works at once is referenced by each of those works.",
